content.text:
Now boss bar CSS. Make name centered above bar with phase beside in small caps on right? Let's restyle:

```
#bossBar{top:96px; width:min(52vw,620px)}
.boss-head{justify-content:center; gap:10px; align-items:center;}
#bossName{font-size:22px; letter-spacing:.2em;}
#bossPhase{font-size:9px; padding:2px 7px; border:1px solid rgba(255,180,140,.35); border-radius:2px; background:rgba(20,8,8,.5);}
.boss-track{height:9px;...}
```
Center makes it look intentional. Maybe place under compass at top 96. Zone title around 37; boss at 96 okay.

Also add a hairline "boss bar" glow. Let's edit.

